WEBVTT


00:02:21.914 --> 00:02:24.576
[ Growls ]


00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.934
[ Shrieks ]


00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:51.701
[ Growling ]


00:02:57.282 --> 00:02:59.876
[ Roaring ]


00:02:59.952 --> 00:03:03.547
[ Howling ]


00:03:20.639 --> 00:03:23.472
[ Growls ]


00:03:26.812 --> 00:03:29.906
[ Animals Yipping ]


00:04:03.182 --> 00:04:05.173
[ Man ]
Hang on now.Just hang on now, baby.


00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.377
- Take it slow. Take it slow.
- Hello, and welcome to-


00:04:07.452 --> 00:04:09.386
-Just take it slow.
- [ Retching ]


00:04:09.454 --> 00:04:11.854
Hi. Tom Newman.
Can you take this, please?


00:04:11.924 --> 00:04:14.688
- Yeah. Hi.
- Thank you. You gonna live?


00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.751
Yeah, now I'm on solid ground.


00:04:16.828 --> 00:04:20.229
I can't tell you how grateful I am you waited
till you got out of it before you puked.


00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:22.893
- Now I'm gonna puke.
- Be nice.


00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:26.699
- I love you.
- David, stop it. David, knock it off!.


00:04:26.772 --> 00:04:28.763
- Stop it.
- David, don't bug your sister.


00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.774
What'd I do?


00:04:30.842 --> 00:04:34.539
David, don't bug pretty girls because they
won't pay attention to you later on in life.


00:04:34.613 --> 00:04:37.912
- Uh, the car's right there.
- Great.


00:04:37.983 --> 00:04:40.383
- Is that our ride?
- [ Man ] Yes.


00:04:40.452 --> 00:04:42.386
Sweet!


00:04:42.454 --> 00:04:44.388
[ Laughing ]


00:04:44.456 --> 00:04:46.447
- Who wants front seat?
- [ David ] Me.


00:04:46.525 --> 00:04:48.618
All right. You got it.Jump in.


00:04:48.694 --> 00:04:50.628
All right.


00:04:53.999 --> 00:04:56.627
Got it? Here.
Okay. Come on,Jess.


00:04:56.702 --> 00:04:58.863
- How do you get in?
- You just climb up,Jess.


00:04:58.937 --> 00:05:01.428
- I'm wearing a skirt.
- I'm not gonna look. I'm your dad.


00:05:01.506 --> 00:05:05.135
Let's just jump in here, or we'll be here all day.
For crying out loud.


00:05:16.154 --> 00:05:18.088
Look at that!


00:05:18.156 --> 00:05:21.319
[ Tom ] David, look at the zebra.
Look at the zebra. See him in there?


00:05:21.393 --> 00:05:24.089
- Look. Right through there.
- Yeah.


00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:44.372
[ Tom ] So, is everyone
having a good time? David?


00:05:44.449 --> 00:05:47.247
- Yeah, it's awesome.
- Good.Jess?


00:05:47.319 --> 00:05:49.253
Hello!


00:05:50.322 --> 00:05:52.347
- I'm sorry. What's your name?
- Mike.


00:05:52.424 --> 00:05:55.154
Mike. Mike, how far is it
to Lake Kadimba by chopper?


00:05:55.227 --> 00:05:58.196
Oh, about two hours. They'll come
pick you up in the morning though.


00:05:58.263 --> 00:06:00.823
- Okay.
- Hey, David! Look over there!


00:06:00.899 --> 00:06:02.799
Look at that!


00:06:04.102 --> 00:06:06.036
[ David ]
Wow!


00:06:07.873 --> 00:06:10.740
[ Trumpets ]


00:06:10.809 --> 00:06:13.039
It's beautiful, isn't it?


00:06:13.111 --> 00:06:15.272
-Jess, hey, sweetie. Look!
- What?


00:06:17.349 --> 00:06:19.340
So what?
I've seen one at the zoo.


00:06:23.121 --> 00:06:25.555
[ Chuckles ]


00:06:29.361 --> 00:06:31.352
[ Chattering ]


00:06:34.933 --> 00:06:37.265
Look at her. It's pathetic!


00:06:37.336 --> 00:06:40.066
Could that bathing suit
be any skimpier? My God!


00:06:40.138 --> 00:06:43.073
Somebody needs to tell her
she's not 1 6 anymore.


00:06:44.142 --> 00:06:46.201
- Hey, not so loud.
- kk [ Rock ]


00:06:46.278 --> 00:06:49.577
- You're talking too loud.
- So what?


00:06:52.718 --> 00:06:54.652
Hey.


00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:56.654
- Mmm.
- Hmm.


00:06:56.722 --> 00:06:58.656
- It's paradise.
- I told you so.


00:06:58.724 --> 00:07:01.887
- Want a taste of something wonderful?
- Yeah.


00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.861
- Mmm.
- You like that?


00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:06.727
[ Groans ]
My God.


00:07:06.798 --> 00:07:09.289
Don't tell me they're
gonna have sex in the pool.


00:07:09.368 --> 00:07:11.768
- You do? [ Laughing ]
- Yeah.


00:07:24.116 --> 00:07:26.050
- Thank you.
- Thank you.


00:07:26.118 --> 00:07:28.279
- David, try this.
- What is it?


00:07:28.353 --> 00:07:30.913
Well, the Zulu call it itibani.


00:07:30.989 --> 00:07:33.321
- Itibani?
- Yeah.


00:07:33.392 --> 00:07:35.724
- What does that mean?
- Warthog.


00:07:35.794 --> 00:07:37.785
- [ Chuckles ]
- [ David ] Warthog?


00:07:37.863 --> 00:07:40.195
[ Tom ]
Check it out. You'll like it.


00:07:41.333 --> 00:07:43.267
Yes?


00:07:45.203 --> 00:07:47.467
Tastes like chicken.


00:07:47.539 --> 00:07:50.167
Chicken? [ Chuckles ]
Tell the warthog that.


00:07:50.242 --> 00:07:52.802
Jess, want to try some?


00:07:52.878 --> 00:07:57.611
- No, thanks, Dad.
I'm your daughter, the vegetarian.
- Right.


00:07:57.682 --> 00:08:00.674
I don't eat characters from The Lion King,
especially not Pumbaa.


00:08:00.752 --> 00:08:02.982
- [ Chuckles ]
- What's so funny?


00:08:04.756 --> 00:08:07.816
Uh, nothing. I-


00:08:07.893 --> 00:08:12.125
- I just thought it was funny. That's all.
- Well, it's not, okay?


00:08:14.199 --> 00:08:17.794
Hang on. Hey, hey, hey, hey.
Let me do it.


00:08:26.344 --> 00:08:28.710
Jess.


00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:32.181
You gotta cut your old dad
some slack here, honey.


00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:34.878
What's going on with this?


00:08:34.953 --> 00:08:36.887
- I hate it here.
- Okay.


00:08:36.955 --> 00:08:40.948
I hate the dust. I hate the heat.
I hate the stupid animals and-


00:08:41.026 --> 00:08:43.688
- [ Sighs ]
- And?


00:08:43.762 --> 00:08:45.821
Why did you have to marry her?


00:08:45.897 --> 00:08:48.297
Jessica, I fell in love with her.
I love her.


00:08:48.366 --> 00:08:52.496
- I thought you loved Mom.
- I do love your mom, but not
the way married people do.


00:08:52.571 --> 00:08:55.062
See, sometimes things change,
people change.


00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:59.076
- Your mom is okay with it-
- I love you. I love Mom.
I want it to stay that way.


00:08:59.144 --> 00:09:01.874
I know you do, but it's not
gonna stay that way, honey.


00:09:01.947 --> 00:09:04.177
- It can't-
- I wanna go home.


00:09:04.249 --> 00:09:06.740
I know you wanna go home, baby.
You can't go home.


00:09:06.818 --> 00:09:10.618
Look, you got a perfect opportunity
just to get to know Amy a little bit.


00:09:10.689 --> 00:09:12.919
I don't want to.


00:09:19.598 --> 00:09:21.998
I want to go home.


00:09:22.067 --> 00:09:25.628
She doesn't want to be your mother.
She doesn't want to be your best friend.


00:09:25.704 --> 00:09:28.434
She just wants a chance.


00:09:30.175 --> 00:09:32.109
- Honey,just give her-
- I want to go home.


00:09:32.177 --> 00:09:34.668
[ Sighs ]


00:09:34.746 --> 00:09:37.738
- Oh, baby.
- I want to go home.


00:09:37.816 --> 00:09:40.751
[Jessica Crying ]


00:09:43.788 --> 00:09:46.120
I just want to go home.


00:09:52.797 --> 00:09:56.631
- [ Amy ] I think this was a mistake.
- [ Tom ] What was a mistake?


00:09:56.701 --> 00:09:59.329
Coming here. This trip.


00:09:59.404 --> 00:10:01.463
Forcing it.


00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.940
Honey, you two guys
had to get together sometime.


00:10:04.009 --> 00:10:06.341
How long were you gonna put it off?


00:10:06.411 --> 00:10:09.903
Look. We're married,
and she's just gotta get used to it.


00:10:09.981 --> 00:10:13.382
I mean, what can I say?
She's a 1 4-year-old teenage girl.


00:10:13.451 --> 00:10:16.511
Yeah. She's scarier
than any animal out here.


00:10:16.588 --> 00:10:20.490
- I promise you that.
- [ Laughs ] Frightening.


00:10:20.559 --> 00:10:24.051
But she'll get over it.
I promise you.


00:10:24.129 --> 00:10:26.654
[ Kisses ]
What can I do to make it better?


00:10:26.731 --> 00:10:29.700
Mmm.
[ Laughing ]


00:10:29.768 --> 00:10:32.965
What can I do to make it better?
[ Kisses ]


00:10:42.747 --> 00:10:46.740
The eland, David, has a long nose
and it has four legs.


00:10:46.818 --> 00:10:50.948
And a gazelle has- I don't know-
the same thing. What the heck.


00:10:51.022 --> 00:10:53.513
- There he is. Hey!
- Good morning.


00:10:53.592 --> 00:10:55.958
- How are you?
- Yeah, I'm doing well. And yourself?.


00:10:56.027 --> 00:10:58.962
- It's Brian, right?
- Yeah, that's right. Good morning. Sleep well?


00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:01.521
- Good morning. Yeah.
- Good. So you ready for our game drive?


00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.591
Why does it have to be so early?


00:11:03.668 --> 00:11:05.795
It is the best time to view the animals.


00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.361
Once the sun's up,
it's gonna just get way too hot.


00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:12.536
- I'd rather be sleeping.
- Oh, I don't think so.


00:11:14.346 --> 00:11:17.338
- So, let's get going. Come on.
- Let's do it.


00:11:17.415 --> 00:11:19.815
- I wish you were coming.
- I work. You play.


00:11:19.884 --> 00:11:23.217
I love you.


00:11:23.288 --> 00:11:25.882
-[ David ] Can I sit in the front?
- Can he sit in front?


00:11:25.957 --> 00:11:28.016
- Sure.
- After you.


00:11:28.093 --> 00:11:30.357
Give Dad a hug. All right!


00:11:30.428 --> 00:11:32.419
Watch your head.


00:11:33.698 --> 00:11:35.689
Okay, now, the two of you...


00:11:35.767 --> 00:11:38.861
try against all your natural instincts
to have a nice time.


00:11:38.937 --> 00:11:42.703
Okay? Don't bug your sister.


00:11:42.774 --> 00:11:45.937
- Bye-bye.
- So this should be fun, right?


00:11:47.579 --> 00:11:49.513
No? Okay.


00:12:13.505 --> 00:12:16.497
Guys, take a look. That over there-
that's the Crocodile River.


00:12:16.574 --> 00:12:19.168
[ Amy ]
It's not much of a river, is it?


00:12:19.244 --> 00:12:22.179
You should see it after the first summer rains.
It's teeming with wildlife.


00:12:22.247 --> 00:12:24.579
- Are there crocodiles?
- Sure.


00:12:28.586 --> 00:12:33.216
Are we actually gonna see some animals,
or are you just gonna talk about 'em all day?


00:12:33.291 --> 00:12:35.282
Well, how about we do
some off-roading then?


00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:39.387
- I thought we were off-roading.
- No, I mean off off-roading.


00:12:40.865 --> 00:12:43.060
Hold on, guys.


00:12:54.679 --> 00:12:57.147
- Um, Mr. Ranger?
- Yeah, buddy?


00:12:57.215 --> 00:13:00.378
- I gotta go.
- Go where?


00:13:00.452 --> 00:13:02.420
Go.


00:13:02.487 --> 00:13:04.614
[ Chuckles ]
All right. Hold on.


00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.463
[ Quiet Growl ]


00:13:19.971 --> 00:13:23.463
So you said you've gotta go?
[ Chuckles ]


00:13:23.541 --> 00:13:25.634
- There it is.
- Oh, no way.


00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:28.838
- What's the matter? Take it.
- No, thanks.


00:13:28.913 --> 00:13:32.440
- Why?
- I don't need to pee.


00:13:32.517 --> 00:13:34.508
- Come on then. Let's go.
- Whoa.


00:13:34.586 --> 00:13:37.077
Brian, do you think
this is a good idea?


00:13:37.155 --> 00:13:40.454
- With him like this, I think it's a very good idea.
- I mean for safety reasons.


00:13:40.525 --> 00:13:44.757
I've got the rifle. He'll be fine,
and so will you two. We'll see you now.


00:13:44.829 --> 00:13:48.458
All right. Let's go find a bush for you
to go do what you need to do.


00:13:48.533 --> 00:13:50.524
- Is that okay?
- Yeah.


00:13:50.602 --> 00:13:52.661
They won't see you.
I promise you. You'll be fine.


00:13:52.737 --> 00:13:57.367
Go behind this tree over here. Give me a shout
when you're done and I'll keep an eye out.


00:14:05.617 --> 00:14:07.983
Um, excuse me?


00:14:08.052 --> 00:14:10.953
- What's up?
- I don't have any toilet paper.


00:14:11.022 --> 00:14:13.354
- But you've got grass. Use it.
- Grass?


00:14:13.424 --> 00:14:17.155
- David, you're in Africa. In Africa-
- [ Growling ]


00:14:17.228 --> 00:14:20.391
What is it?


00:14:24.269 --> 00:14:26.567
Look,Jessica, I know this is hard.


00:14:26.638 --> 00:14:30.665
- It's hard for both of us, but if we could just-
- Something's wrong.


00:14:30.742 --> 00:14:33.176
- I know. That's what I'm saying.
- No. Something is wrong!


00:14:33.244 --> 00:14:35.075
Oh, my God.


00:14:37.148 --> 00:14:39.139
[ Gasps ]


00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.554
[ Growling ]


00:14:46.891 --> 00:14:49.359
[ Sniffing ]


00:14:49.427 --> 00:14:51.622
Get behind me.


00:14:53.064 --> 00:14:54.998
[ Growling ]


00:14:56.901 --> 00:14:59.699
- Oh, my God.
- [ Growls ]


00:14:59.771 --> 00:15:03.571
- Oh, my God! There's another one!
- David!


00:15:16.321 --> 00:15:18.846
Good.


00:15:20.358 --> 00:15:23.122
Where is it? Shit!


00:15:23.194 --> 00:15:25.059
- What?
- He took the keys!


00:15:25.129 --> 00:15:28.064
David, when I tell you to move,
we're gonna go backwards together.


00:15:35.206 --> 00:15:36.764
David!


00:15:36.841 --> 00:15:38.900
- David!
- [ Banging On Window ]


00:15:38.977 --> 00:15:41.104
David!


00:15:41.179 --> 00:15:43.739
David! David!


00:15:43.815 --> 00:15:46.909
David!


00:15:46.985 --> 00:15:50.113
- Why isn't it working?
- It has to be on,Jess.


00:15:50.188 --> 00:15:52.486
Do something!


00:15:52.557 --> 00:15:55.958
David! David!


00:15:56.027 --> 00:15:58.291
- Hey!
- What are you doing?


00:15:58.363 --> 00:16:01.662
Hey! Over here! Over here!


00:16:01.733 --> 00:16:04.566
- Hey!
- [ Growls ]


00:16:04.636 --> 00:16:06.831
Over here!


00:16:08.139 --> 00:16:11.302
- Over here!
- [ Roars ]


00:16:14.879 --> 00:16:16.744
Run! Run!


00:16:18.082 --> 00:16:20.915
[ Gunshot ]


00:16:20.985 --> 00:16:24.944
David! It's coming!


00:16:25.023 --> 00:16:27.457
- Oh, my God.
- It's coming!


00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:31.924
- Open the door,Jess!
- [ Gunshot ]


00:16:31.996 --> 00:16:35.193
- Open the door!
- It won't open!


00:16:35.266 --> 00:16:37.427
Open the door! Open the door!


00:16:44.242 --> 00:16:46.176
- Hurry up! Push!
- David!


00:16:46.244 --> 00:16:49.008
[ Amy ]
Hurry up! Get in!


00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.548
- [ Growling ]
- Come on! Quick! Get in!


00:16:51.616 --> 00:16:53.982
[ Amy Screams ]


00:16:55.553 --> 00:16:58.044
- [ Brian Shouts ]
- Oh, my God!


00:16:59.924 --> 00:17:02.552
- [ Grunts ]
- [Jessica Screaming ]


00:17:04.762 --> 00:17:08.698
- Oh, my God! It's killing him!
- [ Roaring ]


00:17:13.104 --> 00:17:16.870
[ Screaming, Grunting ]


00:17:23.414 --> 00:17:25.712
Oh! Help me.


00:17:25.783 --> 00:17:28.251
[Jessica Crying ]


00:17:28.319 --> 00:17:31.049
Oh, my God!


00:17:31.122 --> 00:17:33.056
[ Screaming ]


00:17:33.124 --> 00:17:36.321
- [ Amy ] Close your eyes!
- [Jessica Screams ]


00:17:37.328 --> 00:17:40.729
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.


00:17:40.798 --> 00:17:43.699
Stay down. Stay down, okay?


00:17:43.768 --> 00:17:45.702
Oh, my God.


00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.170
[Jessica Whimpering ]


00:18:00.952 --> 00:18:03.011
[Jessica Screams ]


00:18:03.087 --> 00:18:05.112
- Oh, my God.
- Don't look!


00:18:08.426 --> 00:18:11.020
[Jessica Crying ]


00:18:17.835 --> 00:18:19.598
[ Machinery Humming ]


00:18:22.373 --> 00:18:27.470
From the north and in the south-
here, take a look at this.


00:18:27.545 --> 00:18:31.743
- I'm talking about here and here, okay?
- Yeah. Okay.


00:18:44.662 --> 00:18:46.687
[Jessica Crying ]


00:18:51.636 --> 00:18:54.662
- Come on.
- [ Crying Continues ]


00:18:58.142 --> 00:19:01.305
[ Beeping ]


00:19:06.317 --> 00:19:09.844
- What?
- There's no signal.


00:19:10.888 --> 00:19:13.083
Great. We're screwed.


00:19:13.157 --> 00:19:15.148
We're not screwed.


00:19:15.226 --> 00:19:19.526
In case you haven't noticed,
our guide was just eaten by a lion.


00:19:19.597 --> 00:19:23.089
If you don't think we're screwed,
you're just as stupid as my mother said you are.


00:19:28.072 --> 00:19:30.632
And we're lost.


00:19:34.612 --> 00:19:37.274
We're not lost.
Your dad will find us.


00:19:37.348 --> 00:19:40.044
- How? We're already off the main road.
- I don't know.


00:19:40.118 --> 00:19:42.586
They'll follow the tracks.


00:19:44.122 --> 00:19:46.989
When we don't show up at the lodge,
they'll- they'll find us.


00:19:47.058 --> 00:19:51.518
- We'll be dead by then.
- No. No.


00:19:51.596 --> 00:19:54.656
- They're gonna eat us! They're gonna eat us.
- No, honey, no.


00:19:54.732 --> 00:19:58.532
They're not gonna eat us. Your dad is gonna
find us. They're gonna follow the tracks.


00:19:58.603 --> 00:20:00.537
- [ Roaring ]
- [ Screaming ]


00:20:00.605 --> 00:20:02.664
Stay down. Stay down.


00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:07.302
Oh, my God! It's on the roof!.
[ Screaming ]


00:20:07.378 --> 00:20:09.346
Oh, my God!


00:20:09.413 --> 00:20:11.244
[ Screams ]


00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:15.647
No! No! Oh, my God.


00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:24.251
- [ Roars ]
- Oh! Oh!


00:20:28.933 --> 00:20:31.163
[ Screaming Continues ]


00:20:37.909 --> 00:20:41.345
[ Screaming ]


00:20:41.412 --> 00:20:45.280
[ Whimpering, Screaming ]


00:20:45.349 --> 00:20:47.510
[ Growling ]


00:20:50.288 --> 00:20:53.052
- Oh, my God.
- No! [ Screaming ]


00:21:03.434 --> 00:21:06.403
- Shh. Shh.
- [ Whimpering ]


00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.961
[Jessica ]
Oh, my God.


00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.975
- [ Rattling ]
- [ Screaming ]


00:21:12.043 --> 00:21:13.943
Oh, my God.


00:21:14.011 --> 00:21:15.945
Oh, my God.


00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:23.413
Stay down, honey.
Don't move. Don't move. Shh.


00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:44.967
Shh.


00:21:47.378 --> 00:21:49.710
[ Growling ]


00:21:55.486 --> 00:21:58.148
[ Ranting ]


00:22:08.165 --> 00:22:10.463
I think they've gone.


00:22:13.771 --> 00:22:16.740
- All of'em?
- Yeah. All of'em.


00:22:16.807 --> 00:22:19.298
It's okay, David. Come on.


00:22:19.377 --> 00:22:23.438
Come on. They've gone.


00:22:28.953 --> 00:22:31.547
What about... the ranger?


00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:36.526
- He's dead.
- Dead?


00:22:38.029 --> 00:22:40.395
Then how are we getting out of here?


00:22:41.732 --> 00:22:44.223
- We're not.
-Jessica.


00:22:47.905 --> 00:22:49.839
Come here.


00:23:27.712 --> 00:23:30.044
[Jessica ]
We need to get the rifle.


00:23:31.215 --> 00:23:34.150
No one's getting out of the car.


00:23:35.152 --> 00:23:37.120
But we need it.


00:23:37.188 --> 00:23:39.679
I don't care. The answer's no.


00:23:42.259 --> 00:23:44.193
[ Whispers ]
I'm thirsty.


00:23:45.629 --> 00:23:47.563
I know.


00:23:47.631 --> 00:23:50.759
But we only have half a bottle of water.
I think we should save it.


00:23:50.835 --> 00:23:52.769
Yeah.


00:23:59.143 --> 00:24:02.635
Here.Just have a sip, okay?


00:24:02.713 --> 00:24:04.408
Jess, you want some water?


00:24:13.691 --> 00:24:16.455
- You still have to go to the bathroom?
- No.


00:24:43.988 --> 00:24:45.922
[ Lion Growls ]


00:24:45.990 --> 00:24:48.424
Why won't they just go away?


00:25:02.506 --> 00:25:04.974
Amy, I'm hungry.


00:25:06.410 --> 00:25:08.344
Yeah, I know.


00:25:08.412 --> 00:25:11.779
First thing we'll do when we get back
is get a big stack of pancakes, okay?


00:25:11.849 --> 00:25:14.283
- And a hamburger.
- [ Amy Chuckles ]


00:25:14.351 --> 00:25:17.514
- Double Quarter Rounder.
- A triple, with fries.


00:25:23.794 --> 00:25:27.195
kk [ Dance ]


00:25:44.281 --> 00:25:45.839
[ Roars ]


00:26:07.738 --> 00:26:09.672
Amy?


00:26:09.740 --> 00:26:12.231
Hello.


00:26:18.449 --> 00:26:21.543
David? Jess!


00:26:22.953 --> 00:26:24.887
- Mr. Newman?
- Hi, Mike.


00:26:24.955 --> 00:26:26.889
It's about your family, sir.


00:26:26.957 --> 00:26:28.652
[ Thunder Rumbling ]


00:26:28.726 --> 00:26:32.218
[ Amy ] Why don't you close your eyes.
We should try to get some rest.


00:26:37.568 --> 00:26:39.559
[ David ]
Can we keep the lights on?


00:26:39.637 --> 00:26:42.731
Well, I don't want to
kill the battery, hon.


00:26:42.806 --> 00:26:46.367
What will we need it for after tonight?
You said they were gonna find us in the morning.


00:26:46.443 --> 00:26:50.038
They are going to find us, but I don't know
how long the battery will last...


00:26:50.114 --> 00:26:52.878
and we might need it
in the middle of the night.


00:27:02.560 --> 00:27:04.551
Are they still there?


00:27:06.230 --> 00:27:09.461
I don't know. I'll check.


00:27:12.002 --> 00:27:14.266
[ Screams ]


00:27:14.338 --> 00:27:16.636
[ Amy ]
It's okay.


00:27:18.042 --> 00:27:19.737
Hey, it's okay.


00:27:21.979 --> 00:27:24.948
Okay, okay. Calm down.


00:27:25.015 --> 00:27:28.246
It's okay, David.
It's okay. Come on.


00:27:28.319 --> 00:27:31.254
- Come on. Come here.
- [ Crying ]


00:27:31.322 --> 00:27:33.449
It's okay.


00:27:33.524 --> 00:27:36.015
It's okay. We're in the car.
Nothing's gonna happen.


00:27:36.093 --> 00:27:38.027
It's okay.


00:27:40.698 --> 00:27:43.826
We're okay in the car, okay?


00:27:43.901 --> 00:27:48.167
- [ Panting ]
- Shh.


00:27:48.238 --> 00:27:50.229
It's okay. It's okay.


00:27:52.376 --> 00:27:55.140
- Nothing's gonna happen.
- [ David Sobs ]


00:27:55.212 --> 00:27:57.373
Shh.


00:27:58.816 --> 00:28:01.148
Shh.


00:28:01.218 --> 00:28:04.676
- It's okay.
- [ Trembling ]


00:28:04.888 --> 00:28:08.346
I'm really sorry, Mr. Newman, but there is
nothing more that we can do right now.


00:28:08.425 --> 00:28:12.759
At least not till morning. If they're
not back by then, we will start searching.


00:28:12.830 --> 00:28:16.288
What are we supposed to do till then,
just sit around with our thumb up our ass?


00:28:16.367 --> 00:28:19.029
Uh, I don't think you have
much of a choice there.


00:28:19.103 --> 00:28:21.037
Our chopper doesn't fly at night.


00:28:21.105 --> 00:28:23.903
- Then why aren't we searching on the ground?
- We're trying.


00:28:23.974 --> 00:28:27.171
Ma'am, why aren't we in a vehicle
searching on the ground?


00:28:27.244 --> 00:28:29.474
We are, but a couple of torches
aren't gonna do much.


00:28:31.548 --> 00:28:34.915
We really do have to wait
until first light, I'm afraid.


00:28:34.985 --> 00:28:37.647
Remarkable.


00:28:37.721 --> 00:28:40.212
Absolutely remarkable.


00:28:41.291 --> 00:28:44.749
Look. Wait. Um-


00:28:44.828 --> 00:28:48.093
There is someone that I know of
who could possibly help you.


00:28:48.165 --> 00:28:53.000
Echo Charlie Zero,
this is Leopard's Rest Lodge. Over.


00:28:56.473 --> 00:28:58.532
Crawford, are you there?


00:29:00.811 --> 00:29:03.336
[ Man ]
Roger there. Shoot.


00:29:03.414 --> 00:29:05.348
Good luck.


00:29:05.416 --> 00:29:08.579
Hello, Mr. Crawford.
My name is Tom Newman.


00:29:08.652 --> 00:29:10.984
I'm a guest at Leopard's Rest Lodge.


00:29:11.055 --> 00:29:13.615
My wife and two children
have been missing since this afternoon.


00:29:13.691 --> 00:29:15.682
Missing?


00:29:15.759 --> 00:29:19.695
Yes, that's right. They were on a game drive,
and they haven't come back yet.


00:29:19.763 --> 00:29:22.288
That's nice. Try the police.


00:29:22.366 --> 00:29:24.891
No, no, no. The police aren't gonna
get here till tomorrow morning.


00:29:24.968 --> 00:29:29.371
Sorry. Can't help you.
If you want a guided hunt, I'm your man.


00:29:29.440 --> 00:29:31.431
If you want to find somebody,
call the rangers.


00:29:31.508 --> 00:29:33.567
I'm with the rangers now,
Mr. Crawford.


00:29:33.644 --> 00:29:37.410
- I'm talking to you from a ranger radio.
- I'd wait till after the rain.


00:29:37.481 --> 00:29:42.214
Hello? Rain? What rain?


00:29:42.286 --> 00:29:45.221
Hello! Ra-


00:29:46.390 --> 00:29:48.324
What rain?


00:29:48.392 --> 00:29:51.054
[ Rain Falling ]


00:29:55.132 --> 00:29:58.033
[ Thunder Rumbling ]


00:30:22.092 --> 00:30:24.583
[ Thunderclap ]


00:30:54.191 --> 00:30:56.682
Whoa. What are you doing?


00:30:56.760 --> 00:31:00.196
- Close the door.
- I'm thirsty.


00:31:00.264 --> 00:31:02.960
I'm thirsty.


00:31:05.335 --> 00:31:08.793
Okay.Just be quick, okay?


00:31:16.947 --> 00:31:20.212
[ Growling ]


00:31:41.972 --> 00:31:44.236
- [ Gasping ]
- [ Amy ] Oh, my God!


00:31:48.011 --> 00:31:51.378
Are you okay? You all right?


00:32:18.876 --> 00:32:22.505
I've got your cell number, so just keep it charged.
I'll phone you when we find them.


00:32:22.579 --> 00:32:25.104
- Phone me? I'm coming with you!
- Only room for two in there.


00:32:25.182 --> 00:32:28.310
- What am I gonna do, stay here?
- There's coffee in the kitchen.


00:32:28.385 --> 00:32:30.683
- I'll call you.
- Are you kidding?


00:33:12.095 --> 00:33:14.495
Where do I find this guy Crawford?


00:33:49.466 --> 00:33:52.731
The keys! It's the keys!


00:33:52.803 --> 00:33:54.737
[ Groans ]
Where?


00:33:54.805 --> 00:33:56.773
Over there! Look!


00:33:58.976 --> 00:34:03.413
Oh, I don't know. It could be an old can
or a piece of glass, babe.


00:34:08.752 --> 00:34:11.880
No! It is the keys. Look.


00:34:14.458 --> 00:34:16.449
Let me see.


00:34:19.696 --> 00:34:21.960
We're saved! We're saved!


00:34:22.032 --> 00:34:24.193
- We have to get 'em first, buddy.
- I'll go.


00:34:24.267 --> 00:34:27.259
No.Jess! No.
You're staying in the car.


00:34:27.337 --> 00:34:30.500
What are you talking about?
The lions are gone, and I'm much faster than you.


00:34:30.574 --> 00:34:34.135
That doesn't matter.
I'm going, and that's final.


00:34:34.211 --> 00:34:37.271
Nothing you say is final.


00:34:37.347 --> 00:34:39.577
Okay.


00:34:39.649 --> 00:34:44.211
When this is all over, you and I are gonna
sit down and have a long conversation.


00:34:44.287 --> 00:34:47.347
But until then, you stay in the car.


00:34:47.424 --> 00:34:49.358
[ Sighs ]


00:34:55.599 --> 00:34:57.931
Don't leave us!


00:34:58.001 --> 00:35:01.300
Hey. You want to
get out of here, right?


00:35:02.773 --> 00:35:06.732
Okay. I'll be back in the blink of an eye.
I promise.


00:35:21.992 --> 00:35:24.222
[ Quiet Growl ]


00:35:43.213 --> 00:35:46.273
[ Growling ]


00:35:55.826 --> 00:35:58.158
[ Growling ]


00:36:10.373 --> 00:36:12.603
- Oh, shit.
- What?


00:36:12.676 --> 00:36:15.110
- [ Growls ]
- Amy!


00:36:15.178 --> 00:36:18.045
- Run! Amy, run!
- Run, Amy!


00:36:18.115 --> 00:36:20.049
[ David ]
Run!


00:36:25.689 --> 00:36:28.055
- [ Roars ]
- Run, Amy!


00:36:31.862 --> 00:36:34.330
Amy! Run!


00:36:34.397 --> 00:36:36.456
Amy!


00:36:38.568 --> 00:36:40.297
Amy!


00:36:40.370 --> 00:36:42.065
[ David ]
Run, Amy!


00:36:46.810 --> 00:36:48.334
[ Amy ]
Oh,Jesus!


00:36:49.980 --> 00:36:52.676
- [ Lion Snarling ]
- [Jessica ] Go, Amy! It's right there!


00:36:52.749 --> 00:36:55.240
- Go!
- Shit.


00:36:55.318 --> 00:36:57.149
- [ Roars ]
- [ Screams ]


00:36:57.220 --> 00:37:00.087
- Amy!
- Amy!


00:37:01.057 --> 00:37:03.525
[ Screams ]
Go, Amy!


00:37:06.396 --> 00:37:08.387
- [ Engine Starts ]
- Come on, Amy!


00:37:09.666 --> 00:37:13.397
Okay! Shift it into first. Okay.


00:37:13.470 --> 00:37:15.904
- Now go!
- Going!


00:37:15.972 --> 00:37:17.906
Go!


00:37:31.788 --> 00:37:34.723
- Watch out!
-[ Amy Grunts ] Get out ofhere!


00:37:36.293 --> 00:37:38.261
God!


00:37:38.328 --> 00:37:40.296
Hold on!


00:37:40.363 --> 00:37:42.627
[ Screams ]


00:37:44.201 --> 00:37:47.136
Let me navigate. Go right!


00:37:47.204 --> 00:37:49.729
[Jessica Screams ]


00:37:49.806 --> 00:37:51.899
Watch out! Go right!


00:37:59.983 --> 00:38:02.577
- We're gonna crash.
- Hold on,Jess.


00:38:02.652 --> 00:38:04.779
- You're going too fast!
- Hold on!


00:38:10.393 --> 00:38:12.258
[ Amy ]
Hold on!


00:38:12.329 --> 00:38:15.765
[ All Screaming ]


00:38:16.800 --> 00:38:19.462
[Jessica ]
Stop the car, Amy!


00:38:32.949 --> 00:38:37.147
Don't get your hopes up. You think you can
handle anyone, but you don't know this guy.


00:38:37.220 --> 00:38:39.484
He's a good hunter though,
the best in the region.


00:38:39.556 --> 00:38:42.684
He doesn't know a thing about people.
Well, this is it.


00:38:42.759 --> 00:38:44.750
- [ Tom ] Wait for me.
- Like I said, he's nuts.


00:38:44.828 --> 00:38:48.161
- You want to do this, you're on your own.
- Hey! Hey! Hey!


00:38:48.231 --> 00:38:50.165
Hey! Hey!


00:38:55.739 --> 00:38:57.673
Mr. Crawford!


00:38:59.442 --> 00:39:01.376
Mr. Crawford?


00:39:01.444 --> 00:39:03.378
Anybody home?


00:39:04.981 --> 00:39:06.915
Mr. Crawford?


00:39:09.019 --> 00:39:11.283
Mr. Crawfor- Mr. Crawford.


00:39:11.354 --> 00:39:16.690
I'm Tom Newman.
We spoke last night on the rangers' radio.


00:39:16.760 --> 00:39:18.694
That's right.


00:39:20.930 --> 00:39:23.091
The rangers find your family?


00:39:23.166 --> 00:39:26.431
- No, they just started looking this morning.
- [ Coughs ]


00:39:26.503 --> 00:39:28.835
Well, I wouldn't hold my breath,
if I were you.


00:39:28.905 --> 00:39:33.205
Exactly. That's why I'm here. I was hoping
maybe that you'd give me some-


00:39:33.276 --> 00:39:35.267
Son of a bitch.


00:39:38.415 --> 00:39:40.178
[ Grunting ]


00:39:43.486 --> 00:39:46.978
Now, I told you,
I lead hunts for the big five...


00:39:47.057 --> 00:39:49.719
not search parties
for wives and kids, pal.


00:39:49.793 --> 00:39:51.761
If you can track a leopard...


00:39:51.828 --> 00:39:55.264
I am sure that three American tourists
will just be a walk in the park for you.


00:39:55.332 --> 00:39:57.323
You're gonna go downhill
appealing to my ego, friend.


00:39:57.400 --> 00:39:59.391
Well, how 'bout I appeal
to your wallet, friend?


00:39:59.469 --> 00:40:01.767
Mr. Crawford...


00:40:01.838 --> 00:40:04.534
I'm the hydroelectrical engineer
supervising the building...


00:40:04.607 --> 00:40:07.576
of the new dam in this province,
and I have money!


00:40:07.644 --> 00:40:10.204
My family's been at large
for more than 2 4 hours.


00:40:10.280 --> 00:40:13.943
And I'm sure that must
just resonate with you a little bit.


00:40:14.017 --> 00:40:18.283
I mean, I'm sure that just must
strike some small chord in you.


00:40:18.355 --> 00:40:20.255
And praying that it does...


00:40:20.323 --> 00:40:24.020
I am prepared to pay you
whatever the hell you want...


00:40:24.094 --> 00:40:27.860
if you just-
if you just help me find my family.


00:40:31.101 --> 00:40:33.626
[ Engine Cranking ]


00:40:36.439 --> 00:40:38.134
Come on!


00:40:40.710 --> 00:40:42.541
Come on!


00:40:42.612 --> 00:40:45.046
[ Cranking ]


00:40:45.115 --> 00:40:47.447
Come on!


00:40:47.517 --> 00:40:49.610
[ Sobs ]


00:40:49.686 --> 00:40:51.677
[ Crying ]


00:40:59.362 --> 00:41:01.660
So, what are we gonna do now?


00:41:01.731 --> 00:41:04.222
[ Crying ]


00:41:10.473 --> 00:41:12.464
By now your dad knows we're missing.


00:41:12.542 --> 00:41:15.443
He probably sent somebody to find us.


00:41:15.512 --> 00:41:19.346
- Who?
- I don't know. The lodge people.


00:41:21.017 --> 00:41:22.951
How are they gonna find us?


00:41:25.688 --> 00:41:27.622
What do you mean?


00:41:27.690 --> 00:41:30.181
Well, they'll be looking for us
off the main road.


00:41:30.260 --> 00:41:33.252
Somewhere close to it.
But now we're nowhere near it.


00:41:35.265 --> 00:41:39.326
Maybe we should just get out of the car
and try to find our way back.


00:41:39.402 --> 00:41:43.634
Yeah, except for that
we have no idea where we are.


00:41:43.706 --> 00:41:45.640
[ Sighs ]


00:41:47.510 --> 00:41:49.444
[ Whispers ]
Fuck.


00:41:51.481 --> 00:41:55.474
And they'll have no idea
where we are if we stay here.


00:41:55.552 --> 00:41:58.316
No. We're not gonna
take any chances.


00:41:58.388 --> 00:42:00.481
As long as we stay in this car,
we're safe.


00:42:00.557 --> 00:42:03.151
- And lost!
- Fine. We're lost.


00:42:03.226 --> 00:42:05.626
We're not leaving this car.


00:42:05.695 --> 00:42:09.096
- Why? Because you say so?
- Because it's safe,Jess!


00:42:09.165 --> 00:42:12.794
Because your father is gonna find us,
and, yeah, because I say so!


00:42:12.869 --> 00:42:15.633
- You think he's gonna find us.
- Yes, I do.


00:42:15.705 --> 00:42:18.640
- What if he doesn't find us?
- He will.


00:42:18.708 --> 00:42:20.972
- And if he doesn't?
- He will,Jess.


00:42:21.044 --> 00:42:23.877
- What if my dad doesn't find us?
- Goddamn it, he will!


00:42:26.449 --> 00:42:29.509
[Jessica Crying ]


00:42:48.404 --> 00:42:51.373
[ Tom ]
What are we looking for?


00:42:51.441 --> 00:42:54.706
[ Crawford ] Smoke, vultures in the sky.
You'll know it when you see it.


00:42:54.777 --> 00:42:58.941
I mean, are we looking for some kind
of trail or something, Mr. Crawford?


00:42:59.015 --> 00:43:02.075
Any tracks that would've been left
have been washed away by now.


00:43:09.826 --> 00:43:13.489
- [ Radio Beeping ]
- [ Man ] No luck at Lake Maluti.


00:43:13.563 --> 00:43:16.088
We're heading north.
The roads are empty here.


00:43:16.165 --> 00:43:19.396
Well, of course the roads are empty,
you rabbit. It rained last night.


00:43:19.469 --> 00:43:21.266
You chop in on the ranger frequency?


00:43:21.337 --> 00:43:23.532
Uh, we're gonna drop in periodically...


00:43:23.606 --> 00:43:26.074
and just, uh, fill in the gaps
for those clowns.


00:43:26.142 --> 00:43:28.133
And what exactly are the gaps,
Mr. Crawford?


00:43:28.211 --> 00:43:31.442
Well, they want a quick rescue,
so they've gone up into the air.


00:43:31.514 --> 00:43:35.143
The problem with that is that they
might fly right over your family...


00:43:35.218 --> 00:43:37.618
and not even know it.


00:44:31.841 --> 00:44:35.277
Hey. How you doing?


00:44:35.345 --> 00:44:37.438
- I'm fine.
- Yeah?


00:44:38.748 --> 00:44:40.807
He needs some water.


00:44:40.883 --> 00:44:43.511
Yeah. I know. We all do.


00:44:43.586 --> 00:44:45.713
But he really needs some.


00:44:45.788 --> 00:44:48.985
Let me go find some water.


00:44:49.058 --> 00:44:52.289
Are you crazy?
What about the lions?


00:44:52.362 --> 00:44:55.229
[ Sighs ]
Well, we haven't seen 'em all morning.


00:44:55.298 --> 00:44:57.198
Doesn't mean they're not out there.


00:44:58.534 --> 00:45:00.468
Fine.


00:45:27.463 --> 00:45:29.454
What are you doing?


00:45:31.768 --> 00:45:34.896
There's a little water here
from the storm.


00:45:41.310 --> 00:45:43.301
Here.


00:45:54.590 --> 00:45:56.581
It was a good idea.


00:45:57.660 --> 00:46:00.151
[ Helicopter Approaching, Faint ]


00:46:01.864 --> 00:46:03.855
- What is it?
- Shh.


00:46:05.368 --> 00:46:07.302
[ Helicopter Approaching, Faint ]


00:46:07.370 --> 00:46:09.770
A helicopter.


00:46:09.839 --> 00:46:12.706
- Hey-Jess, no!
- Let go of me!


00:46:12.775 --> 00:46:14.709
What did I tell you?


00:46:14.777 --> 00:46:18.611
- What if they can't see us?
- They'll see us, okay? We're not getting out.


00:46:33.396 --> 00:46:36.490
There's no sign of them
at the Crocodile River.


00:46:36.566 --> 00:46:39.467
We're gonna check the Letaba trails
at the secondary gate.


00:46:44.507 --> 00:46:47.169
- It's leaving.
- No.


00:46:49.512 --> 00:46:52.811
-Jess, no!
- Hey!


00:46:52.882 --> 00:46:57.478
Over here! Help! Come back! Help!


00:46:57.553 --> 00:47:00.488
[ Whimpering ]
Help! Come back!


00:47:00.556 --> 00:47:03.650
Over here! Come back!


00:47:05.094 --> 00:47:07.585
- No. Oh, no.
-Jess!


00:47:07.663 --> 00:47:10.131
- David, close the door.
- No.


00:47:10.199 --> 00:47:12.531
- jess, come back!
- Shit.


00:47:12.602 --> 00:47:14.866
- [ Door Closes ]
- [ Sobbing ]


00:47:16.839 --> 00:47:21.071
- Hey, I'm sorry.
- You should have let me go.
You should have let me go.


00:47:21.144 --> 00:47:24.705
- [ Sobbing Continues ]
- [ Whispering ] We gotta get in the car.


00:47:24.781 --> 00:47:28.945
- We gotta get in the car. We gotta get in the car.
- [ Quiet Growling ]


00:47:30.286 --> 00:47:32.311
- [ Whispering ] I'm sorry.
- [ Sobbing Continues ]


00:47:32.388 --> 00:47:35.380
- [ Rustling ]
- [ Growling Continues ]


00:47:40.429 --> 00:47:42.989
[ Growling Continues ]


00:47:59.215 --> 00:48:01.410
[ Gunshot ]


00:48:16.599 --> 00:48:18.897
[ Men Conversing In Native Language]


00:48:22.672 --> 00:48:25.539
[ Native Language]


00:48:31.647 --> 00:48:34.514
- [ Laughs ]
- [ Native Language ]


00:48:34.584 --> 00:48:36.711
Excuse me.


00:48:36.786 --> 00:48:39.914
Yeah- Can you help us, please?


00:48:43.759 --> 00:48:47.092
- Please. We need your help.
The lions, they attacked us.
- [ Native Language ]


00:48:47.163 --> 00:48:51.964
- They killed our guide. We have no guide.
-Jessica, go to the car.


00:48:52.034 --> 00:48:54.628
[ Native Language ]


00:48:54.704 --> 00:48:57.867
They don't understand
a word I'm saying, do they?


00:48:57.940 --> 00:49:00.636
Go. Lock the car.


00:49:02.245 --> 00:49:04.179
[ Both Chuckling ]


00:49:04.247 --> 00:49:06.374
[ Native Language ]


00:49:20.663 --> 00:49:22.927
[ Flies Buzzing ]


00:49:28.170 --> 00:49:30.104
Who are they?


00:49:30.172 --> 00:49:32.106
Poachers, I think.


00:49:32.174 --> 00:49:34.972
- What are they doing?
- They're skinning a lion.


00:49:35.044 --> 00:49:39.606
- That's disgusting.
- Yeah. Starting to understand
why you're a vegetarian.


00:49:41.517 --> 00:49:44.611
- [Jessica ] So, they're gonna help us, right?
- I don't know.


00:49:44.687 --> 00:49:47.622
They didn't seem to be
too concerned with us, did they?


00:49:47.690 --> 00:49:51.649
I don't know how often this happens, but you
would think we would be of greater interest.


00:49:51.727 --> 00:49:54.890
Maybe they know
where we can find some water.


00:49:55.932 --> 00:49:57.923
Yeah, maybe.


00:50:00.036 --> 00:50:02.027
Rut your sweatshirt on. Okay?


00:50:04.440 --> 00:50:07.432
David, you lock the door
when we get out. Okay?


00:50:07.510 --> 00:50:09.501
Okay.


00:50:22.758 --> 00:50:25.056
- [ Amy ] Excuse me?
- Excuse me.


00:50:25.127 --> 00:50:28.824
Um, water.
Do you have any water?


00:50:28.898 --> 00:50:30.832
- [ Native Language ]
- Water.


00:50:30.900 --> 00:50:33.664
- Uh, like- [ Gulping ]
- [ Native Language ]


00:50:33.736 --> 00:50:37.467
[ Conversing In Native Language]


00:50:39.041 --> 00:50:41.032
[Jessica ]
Do you speak English?


00:50:41.110 --> 00:50:43.408
Can you help us?


00:50:43.479 --> 00:50:45.970
[ Amy ]
Water. W-Water- Yes! Yes!


00:50:46.048 --> 00:50:48.539
- We need water. Please.
- [ Native Language ]


00:50:51.620 --> 00:50:53.611
Can-


00:50:55.624 --> 00:50:58.422
- What is he saying?
- I have no clue.


00:50:58.494 --> 00:51:00.826
[ Native Language ]
Come.


00:51:00.896 --> 00:51:03.888
- You speak English?
- Whoa. What do you think you're doing?


00:51:03.966 --> 00:51:07.402
I'm going to get water for my brother.


00:51:07.470 --> 00:51:09.904
One of us needs to stay with David...


00:51:09.972 --> 00:51:12.907
and one of us needs to go
with Knife Guy here.


00:51:12.975 --> 00:51:14.909
You have a bad ankle.


00:51:14.977 --> 00:51:17.912
Look, I- I just don't think
this is a good idea.


00:51:17.980 --> 00:51:21.245
Amy, you have to trust me.
It'll be fine. Okay?


00:51:21.317 --> 00:51:23.308
It'll be fine.


00:51:57.787 --> 00:52:00.779
Uh, are you sure this is the right way?


00:52:05.861 --> 00:52:09.126
Is it... a lot further...


00:52:09.198 --> 00:52:11.063
up ahead?


00:52:11.133 --> 00:52:13.067
[ Native Language ]


00:52:13.135 --> 00:52:15.126
Yeah.


00:52:21.477 --> 00:52:23.638
[ Whispers ]
What are you doing?


00:52:54.810 --> 00:52:56.801
Thank you.


00:52:59.682 --> 00:53:03.948
Do you have anything that I can carry?


00:53:04.019 --> 00:53:06.487
Carry back?


00:53:06.555 --> 00:53:08.546
Water?


00:53:10.292 --> 00:53:12.886
The water? Carry back?


00:53:14.897 --> 00:53:16.888
Carry?


00:53:54.403 --> 00:53:56.735
[ Wings Flapping ]


00:54:19.428 --> 00:54:22.420
[ Native Language ]


00:54:40.683 --> 00:54:42.617
Um...


00:54:42.685 --> 00:54:44.619
what about the other one?


00:54:44.687 --> 00:54:46.951
Can you cut it up?


00:54:55.764 --> 00:54:57.755
Thank you.


00:55:03.906 --> 00:55:05.840
[ Gunshot ]


00:55:06.575 --> 00:55:09.305
[ Grunting, Snorting ]


00:55:25.361 --> 00:55:27.795
- Shh!
- What? Let go of me!


00:55:27.863 --> 00:55:29.831
- [ Native Language ]
- Let go of me.


00:55:29.898 --> 00:55:32.560
- [ Native Language ]
- What?


00:55:32.635 --> 00:55:34.626
What is it?


00:55:39.608 --> 00:55:42.634
- [ Whispers ] Amy. David.
- Shh.


00:55:45.781 --> 00:55:48.272
[ Native Language ]


00:55:52.121 --> 00:55:54.954
- [ Whispers In Native Language ]
- What?


00:56:26.989 --> 00:56:29.048
Amy?


00:56:29.658 --> 00:56:31.990
Get in the car!


00:56:32.061 --> 00:56:35.224
What are you guys doing?


00:56:35.297 --> 00:56:37.857
- Thank God you're okay.
- What's going on? I heard a gunshot.


00:56:37.933 --> 00:56:40.367
Where are you going?
Get in the car!


00:56:40.436 --> 00:56:42.700
[Jessica ]
Where are you going?


00:56:42.771 --> 00:56:45.501
The lion! It's gonna eat you!


00:56:48.077 --> 00:56:50.944
You can't do anything,Jess.


00:56:51.013 --> 00:56:53.948
You can't do anything.


00:56:54.016 --> 00:56:55.779
- Want some?
- Yeah.


00:56:55.851 --> 00:56:57.842
[ Coughs ]


00:57:14.069 --> 00:57:16.264
- Scat.
- Scat?


00:57:17.306 --> 00:57:19.934
Lion dung.


00:57:20.008 --> 00:57:22.203
Okay.


00:57:22.277 --> 00:57:25.713
Judging by the consistency,
he's eaten recently.


00:57:25.781 --> 00:57:28.409
It's hard to tell what, exactly.


00:57:28.484 --> 00:57:30.475
Okay.


00:57:30.552 --> 00:57:34.784
Since the drought set in,
these guys have had a ferocious appetite.


00:57:34.857 --> 00:57:38.418
So either he's eaten a gazelle, which is good,
because he won't be so hungry-


00:57:38.494 --> 00:57:40.485
Or?


00:57:42.965 --> 00:57:44.956
Or he's eaten something else.


00:57:45.033 --> 00:57:46.967
Like a human?


00:57:47.035 --> 00:57:50.664
Judging by the temperature,
he dumped that a couple of hours ago...


00:57:50.739 --> 00:57:54.505
which means he's pretty far away now.


00:57:54.576 --> 00:57:56.510
So, what do we do now?


00:57:56.578 --> 00:57:58.512
Now? Now we set up camp.


00:57:58.580 --> 00:58:00.514
- Camp?
- That's right.


00:58:00.582 --> 00:58:02.516
'Cause there is not a ranger alive...


00:58:02.584 --> 00:58:05.576
that can find your family
once the sun goes down...


00:58:05.654 --> 00:58:07.747
Mr. Newman.


00:58:37.286 --> 00:58:40.278
[ Growling ]


00:58:58.140 --> 00:59:01.075
Well, I read it in some
wildlife magazine or something.


00:59:01.143 --> 00:59:04.977
Hell, I can't remember where.
But it's rare that they attack people, right?


00:59:05.047 --> 00:59:07.982
What I read was, they're more
afraid of us than we are of them.


00:59:08.050 --> 00:59:10.883
- Right?
- Bullshit.


00:59:10.953 --> 00:59:12.921
A hungry lion'll eat anything.


00:59:46.655 --> 00:59:49.647
kk [ Pop ]


01:00:08.377 --> 01:00:10.368
''[ Stops ]


01:00:28.497 --> 01:00:31.489
Amy? Are you awake?


01:00:33.302 --> 01:00:35.293
No.


01:00:36.338 --> 01:00:38.272
Me too.


01:00:38.340 --> 01:00:40.331
My iPod's dead.


01:00:40.409 --> 01:00:42.400
Sorry.


01:00:46.481 --> 01:00:48.472
Amy?


01:00:50.118 --> 01:00:53.417
- Yeah?
- How'd you meet my dad?


01:00:54.990 --> 01:00:57.925
Oh,Jess, I don't think
I wanna get into that right now.


01:00:57.993 --> 01:00:59.984
No, I just wanna know.


01:01:13.475 --> 01:01:17.377
Well, I was on a plane-


01:01:17.446 --> 01:01:19.004
Mile-high club?


01:01:19.081 --> 01:01:21.208
The mile-high club?


01:01:22.284 --> 01:01:24.275
[ Sighs ]


01:01:24.353 --> 01:01:26.344
-Jesus.
- Sorry.


01:01:28.323 --> 01:01:30.314
Go ahead.


01:01:32.127 --> 01:01:35.722
I was sitting two rows behind him.


01:01:35.797 --> 01:01:38.732
We were on a flight to Chicago...


01:01:38.800 --> 01:01:41.064
and halfway through the flight...


01:01:41.136 --> 01:01:44.401
he came back and asked ifhe could
sit on the empty seat next to me.


01:01:44.473 --> 01:01:47.738
- He approached you?
- Mm-hmm.


01:01:47.809 --> 01:01:50.039
[Jessica ]
Well, what did he want?


01:01:51.213 --> 01:01:53.147
We just started talking.


01:01:53.215 --> 01:01:54.876
Before I knew it...


01:01:54.950 --> 01:01:59.182
the captain had switched on
the ''fasten seat belts'' lights for landing.


01:01:59.254 --> 01:02:01.848
What did you guys talk about?


01:02:01.923 --> 01:02:03.857
Just things.


01:02:03.925 --> 01:02:06.223
His life, my life.


01:02:08.063 --> 01:02:10.054
Things.


01:02:10.132 --> 01:02:12.396
And then?


01:02:12.467 --> 01:02:15.834
And then we landed and-


01:02:19.841 --> 01:02:23.106
The thing was, your dad had
a connecting flight to New York...


01:02:23.178 --> 01:02:26.614
so you can imagine
how surprised I was when I...


01:02:26.682 --> 01:02:29.276
saw him as I was getting into my cab.


01:02:29.351 --> 01:02:31.979
- He got off his flight?
- Yeah.


01:02:32.988 --> 01:02:34.853
Yeah. He had a white lily.


01:02:36.258 --> 01:02:39.386
just a single white lily.


01:02:39.461 --> 01:02:42.055
And then he asked me out to dinner.


01:02:42.130 --> 01:02:46.157
- How cheesy.
- [ Giggles ] Yeah.


01:02:46.234 --> 01:02:49.670
I usually don't fall
for things like that...


01:02:49.738 --> 01:02:52.730
but, God, he was just so...


01:02:52.808 --> 01:02:54.799
persistent, you know.


01:02:58.413 --> 01:03:00.404
Yeah.


01:03:09.791 --> 01:03:12.988
Jess, your parents were separated
when I met your father.


01:03:13.061 --> 01:03:17.259
I promise you that. I would never have
gone out with him ifhe was married.


01:03:17.332 --> 01:03:21.268
I wouldn't be sitting here right now
if he had been.


01:03:21.336 --> 01:03:23.270
Yeah?


01:03:23.338 --> 01:03:25.431
But we are.


01:03:27.275 --> 01:03:29.266
Yeah.


01:03:30.912 --> 01:03:32.903
[ Rustling ]


01:03:38.053 --> 01:03:41.819
- Amy, what is it?
- I don't know. I can't see anything.


01:03:43.925 --> 01:03:46.086
It's too dark.


01:03:52.000 --> 01:03:54.434
- Amy, I can't see anything.
- I know. It's so-


01:03:54.503 --> 01:03:57.597
- [ Screams ]
- What's going on?


01:03:57.672 --> 01:03:59.503
- Let him in!
- [ Native Language ]


01:04:01.409 --> 01:04:04.037
Open!


01:04:04.112 --> 01:04:07.275
- Are you okay?
- What's going on?


01:04:07.349 --> 01:04:09.283
Shh. Shh.


01:04:09.351 --> 01:04:11.444
Oh, my God.
[ Panting ]


01:04:24.032 --> 01:04:27.058
- [ Growling ]
- [ All Screaming ]


01:04:28.303 --> 01:04:31.136
[ Man Screaming ]


01:04:31.206 --> 01:04:33.367
Oh, God! Oh, my God!


01:04:33.441 --> 01:04:36.001
Oh! Oh, my God!


01:04:36.077 --> 01:04:39.069
[ Screaming Continues ]


01:04:45.153 --> 01:04:48.384
Oh, my God! Get down! Get down!


01:04:50.425 --> 01:04:52.518
Oh! No!


01:05:02.170 --> 01:05:05.037
[ Growling Continues ]


01:05:11.913 --> 01:05:14.575
[ Man Screaming ]


01:05:16.484 --> 01:05:20.215
[ Growling Stops ]


01:05:20.288 --> 01:05:23.587
- [ Panting ]
- [ Whimpering ]


01:05:25.927 --> 01:05:29.624
[ Gasping ] Get the seats up!
Barricade the window!


01:05:33.335 --> 01:05:35.326
Get in the back!


01:05:38.473 --> 01:05:40.464
Get down. Get down.


01:06:10.171 --> 01:06:12.036
[Jessica ]
Amy...


01:06:12.107 --> 01:06:14.041
it's been two days...


01:06:14.109 --> 01:06:16.100
and two nights.


01:06:17.379 --> 01:06:19.904
What if nobody comes?


01:06:19.981 --> 01:06:21.972
Tom's coming.


01:06:23.919 --> 01:06:26.012
What if he can't find us?


01:06:26.087 --> 01:06:28.078
Then we wait.


01:06:29.724 --> 01:06:31.715
Wait to starve?


01:06:33.261 --> 01:06:35.752
We don't have a lot of options.


01:06:37.332 --> 01:06:39.823
We need a place
where rescuers can find us.


01:06:39.901 --> 01:06:42.028
Yeah.


01:06:42.103 --> 01:06:44.970
How do you plan
to fend off the lions? Huh?


01:06:46.808 --> 01:06:48.799
Maybe they're full.


01:06:48.877 --> 01:06:51.311
''Maybe they're full''?


01:06:53.748 --> 01:06:56.216
Maybe they found someone else to eat.


01:06:56.284 --> 01:06:58.878
- Maybe they've given up.
- Maybe they've-


01:06:58.954 --> 01:07:02.355
Yeah, maybe they're just waiting
for us to expose ourselves.


01:07:04.659 --> 01:07:07.093
We need food, we're dehydrated...


01:07:07.162 --> 01:07:10.097
and our one source of protection,
this stupid car...


01:07:10.165 --> 01:07:12.030
is falling to pieces.


01:07:12.100 --> 01:07:15.968
[Jessica ] At some point we're gonna
have to get out of the car and go find help.


01:07:18.306 --> 01:07:22.640
So our only choices right now
are to starve to death...


01:07:22.711 --> 01:07:24.702
or be eaten?


01:07:26.414 --> 01:07:28.405
I don't wanna die here.


01:07:28.483 --> 01:07:31.748
I won't let you die here.


01:07:33.355 --> 01:07:35.721
What are we gonna do?


01:07:48.636 --> 01:07:50.570
[ Sniffles ]


01:07:50.638 --> 01:07:52.606
Okay.
[ Sniffles ]


01:07:52.674 --> 01:07:55.165
Okay.
[ Sniffles ]


01:07:55.243 --> 01:07:59.179
Okay. We just gotta do the best
with what we got. Right?


01:08:05.820 --> 01:08:07.754
We need to...


01:08:07.822 --> 01:08:09.756
barricade that window.


01:08:09.824 --> 01:08:11.758
Right?


01:08:11.826 --> 01:08:14.021
So...


01:08:14.095 --> 01:08:17.690
I want you to just be careful with this.


01:08:17.766 --> 01:08:21.497
I want you to cut the seat belts
and somehow...


01:08:21.569 --> 01:08:24.902
secure those seats
in front of the window.


01:08:24.973 --> 01:08:27.407
- Okay?
- Okay.


01:08:27.475 --> 01:08:29.409
And when you're done...


01:08:29.477 --> 01:08:32.640
let's cut up this carpeting
and put it in front of the windows.


01:08:32.714 --> 01:08:35.239
Shades.
It's too damn hot in here.


01:08:35.316 --> 01:08:38.752
What about me? What can I do?


01:08:38.820 --> 01:08:40.981
You can help me take inventory. Okay?


01:08:41.056 --> 01:08:44.924
I want you to go through every pocket,
every bag, every compartment.


01:08:44.993 --> 01:08:47.962
I wanna know exactly
what we have to work with.


01:08:52.967 --> 01:08:54.958
Mr. Crawford. Mr. Crawford.


01:08:56.638 --> 01:09:00.074
[ Shrieking ]


01:09:01.409 --> 01:09:05.903
[ Growling, Barking ]


01:09:17.392 --> 01:09:19.292
Gross.


01:09:19.360 --> 01:09:22.352
[ Whining ]


01:09:23.765 --> 01:09:27.098
[ Growling ]


01:09:27.168 --> 01:09:30.660
- That one over there just pulled his foot off.
- David, stop looking.


01:09:30.738 --> 01:09:33.104
- But it pulled his foot off.
- David!


01:09:33.174 --> 01:09:36.735
[ Amy ] Why don't you show me
the inventory, huh? Come on.


01:09:38.246 --> 01:09:40.874
[ David ]
Well, I found two black pens...


01:09:40.949 --> 01:09:43.509
an owner's manual, a tool kit...


01:09:43.585 --> 01:09:46.486
some tissues, a road map...


01:09:46.554 --> 01:09:50.012
rubber bands
and cough drop wrappers.


01:09:51.292 --> 01:09:53.453
And I also found this.


01:09:56.564 --> 01:09:58.555
-[Jessica ] That's not mine.
- Yeah, it is.


01:09:58.633 --> 01:10:00.294
David, no, it's not.


01:10:00.368 --> 01:10:02.962
Oh, yeah? Then whose is it?


01:10:08.076 --> 01:10:10.670
It's mine. Okay?


01:10:11.813 --> 01:10:15.408
Sometimes I smoke
when I'm nervous or stressed...


01:10:15.483 --> 01:10:19.146
and I was nervous coming here, and-


01:10:21.422 --> 01:10:24.858
Sometimes you guys
stress me out, so-


01:10:24.926 --> 01:10:27.486
I guess we can be
a little overwhelming at times.


01:10:27.562 --> 01:10:29.894
Yeah. A little.


01:10:29.964 --> 01:10:31.898
[ Laughs ]


01:10:31.966 --> 01:10:35.265
Don't worry.
Your secret's safe with us.


01:10:35.336 --> 01:10:37.327
Thanks.


01:10:40.108 --> 01:10:42.736
Okay, let's put this stuff away.


01:10:45.146 --> 01:10:48.240
- [ Birds Shrieking ]
- Mmm. Mmm.


01:10:51.753 --> 01:10:55.348
Mr. Crawford, that is-
that is not a gazelle.


01:10:55.423 --> 01:10:57.914
Mm-mmm.


01:11:00.628 --> 01:11:02.562
So, what are we looking for?


01:11:02.630 --> 01:11:06.430
The rest of this guy.Just stay tight.
We might have some bigger company.


01:11:06.501 --> 01:11:08.935
[ Whining ]


01:11:09.003 --> 01:11:11.471
That's strange.


01:11:11.539 --> 01:11:15.236
- What?
- They all just left.


01:11:21.816 --> 01:11:24.717
Like they got scared or something.


01:11:24.786 --> 01:11:26.720
Scared?


01:11:26.788 --> 01:11:28.756
[ Growling ]


01:11:36.064 --> 01:11:40.228
- Slowly.Just move back slowly.
- [ Growling Continues ]


01:11:54.549 --> 01:11:57.643
[ Growling Continues ]


01:12:08.496 --> 01:12:10.487
He's leaving!


01:12:13.468 --> 01:12:15.902
[ Vehicle Approaching, Faint ]


01:12:15.970 --> 01:12:18.234
Is that a car?


01:12:19.674 --> 01:12:23.269
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah, that is a car.


01:12:23.344 --> 01:12:25.972
Must be on the other side of the ridge.


01:12:36.324 --> 01:12:38.258
The damn trail's gone cold, man.


01:12:38.326 --> 01:12:40.453
Let's get back to the jeep,
keep driving.


01:12:40.528 --> 01:12:44.191
- We'll pitch camp. Tomorrow we head west.
- Pitch camp?


01:12:44.265 --> 01:12:46.199
Pitch camp.
Tomorrow we head west.


01:12:46.267 --> 01:12:48.394
But you said the rangers
are covering the west.


01:12:48.469 --> 01:12:50.403
There's no point
in covering this area anymore.


01:12:50.471 --> 01:12:54.305
Crawford, you said we're covering the area
that the rangers aren't covering.


01:12:54.375 --> 01:12:58.243
Newman, have you ever
taken heat before, pal? Have you?


01:12:58.313 --> 01:13:03.148
'Cause you'd better come to terms with
the fact that we might never find them.


01:13:05.486 --> 01:13:08.922
- We need to get out of the car
and make some noise.
- What about the lion?


01:13:08.990 --> 01:13:10.981
He's gone!


01:13:12.560 --> 01:13:15.085
Okay. Okay. I'll go to the ridge.


01:13:15.163 --> 01:13:18.428
What are you talking about?
You can't. What about your ankle?


01:13:18.499 --> 01:13:20.933
- I'm going. Okay?
- Absolutely not,Jess.


01:13:21.002 --> 01:13:22.936
You have no say in this.


01:13:23.004 --> 01:13:25.700
Jess, please! Not now! Okay?


01:13:25.773 --> 01:13:28.298
I'm not gonna lose you.


01:13:28.376 --> 01:13:30.401
Okay, well, here. Take my shoes.


01:13:30.478 --> 01:13:32.412
They have more support.


01:13:32.480 --> 01:13:34.380
Jess.


01:13:34.449 --> 01:13:37.782
There's no time. Okay?


01:13:43.791 --> 01:13:45.782
Amy.


01:13:50.698 --> 01:13:52.689
[ Whispers ]
Okay.


01:13:58.172 --> 01:14:02.666
You tourists,you come here and stay
in your posh tents by the pool...


01:14:02.744 --> 01:14:07.340
and you go back home and tell about your
adventure stories like it was a trip to the zoo.


01:14:07.415 --> 01:14:09.883
Well, out here you're the zoo, pal...


01:14:10.985 --> 01:14:14.352
and you'd better
look this thing in the eye.


01:14:15.423 --> 01:14:17.357
Mr. Crawford...


01:14:17.425 --> 01:14:20.758
with or without your help I'm gonna
get in that piece-of-shit vehicle...


01:14:20.828 --> 01:14:24.059
and I'm gonna scour every
goddamned inch of this continent...


01:14:24.132 --> 01:14:26.760
until I find my family.


01:14:28.903 --> 01:14:30.894
[ Amy, Faint ]
Help!


01:14:32.373 --> 01:14:34.568
[ Faint ]
Help! Help us!


01:14:34.642 --> 01:14:36.576
Newman.


01:14:36.644 --> 01:14:38.908
[ Faint ]
Hey! Over here!


01:14:40.848 --> 01:14:42.839
Newman!


01:14:44.552 --> 01:14:46.315
[ Faint ]
Help!


01:14:48.055 --> 01:14:49.784
Over here!


01:14:49.857 --> 01:14:52.951
Over here! Down here!


01:14:53.027 --> 01:14:56.588
Rlease help us!


01:14:56.664 --> 01:14:59.030
Please!


01:15:00.735 --> 01:15:03.260
Down here! Help us!


01:15:03.337 --> 01:15:05.999
Help us! Please!


01:15:07.608 --> 01:15:10.475
Over here!


01:15:10.545 --> 01:15:13.275
Help! Over here!


01:15:17.185 --> 01:15:20.177
Yes! Help us! Help us!


01:15:22.690 --> 01:15:25.989
- [ Crawford ] Oh.
- Help us! Please!


01:15:26.060 --> 01:15:29.325
- Help us!
- It's them. It's them!


01:15:32.767 --> 01:15:35.133
Newman, I think we- Newman!


01:15:41.576 --> 01:15:44.409
[ Snorting ]


01:15:47.915 --> 01:15:50.884
[ Snorting Continues ]


01:15:50.952 --> 01:15:53.944
[ Growling ]


01:16:05.566 --> 01:16:07.500
What is it?


01:16:07.568 --> 01:16:09.559
They're coming down the ridge.


01:16:10.738 --> 01:16:13.298
We'll just let them come to us. Okay?


01:16:24.452 --> 01:16:27.080
- Dad!
- Dad!
- Oh, my God.


01:16:29.423 --> 01:16:32.119
Dad!


01:16:33.861 --> 01:16:36.386
[ Growling ]


01:16:36.464 --> 01:16:39.092
- Dad, there's a lion!
- What?


01:16:39.166 --> 01:16:42.260
- Watch out for the lion!
- A what?


01:16:42.336 --> 01:16:45.464
- Dad!
- There's a lion!


01:16:45.540 --> 01:16:48.703
- Watch out for the lion!
- Watch out, Dad!


01:16:48.776 --> 01:16:51.939
- Tom, don't move.
- What?


01:16:52.013 --> 01:16:54.311
- Don't move, Tom.
- Run, Dad!


01:16:54.382 --> 01:16:56.373
- Run, Tom!
- [ Growling ]


01:17:00.288 --> 01:17:03.815
[ Growling Continues ]


01:17:12.199 --> 01:17:14.394
Shoot it, Mr. Crawford. Please.


01:17:17.672 --> 01:17:19.435
I don't have a shot, pal.


01:17:21.242 --> 01:17:23.802
[ Growling Continues ]


01:17:28.583 --> 01:17:30.642
Dad!


01:17:32.587 --> 01:17:34.919
[ Crawford ]
Tom! Duck!


01:17:34.989 --> 01:17:37.856
- [ Gunshot ]
- [ Gasps ]


01:17:40.494 --> 01:17:43.190
- Dad, get in the car!
- Hurry up!


01:17:43.264 --> 01:17:44.856
[ Amy ]
Hurry up!


01:17:44.932 --> 01:17:47.526
[ Growling ]


01:17:50.705 --> 01:17:53.196
[ Roaring ]


01:18:02.416 --> 01:18:04.145
[ David ]
Dad!


01:18:04.218 --> 01:18:07.051
- Dad!
- Dad!


01:18:07.121 --> 01:18:10.181
- Open the door, David!
- I can't! It's stuck!


01:18:10.257 --> 01:18:12.555
- Run, Dad!
- Open the door!


01:18:13.861 --> 01:18:16.455
Dad! Dad! It's stuck!


01:18:16.530 --> 01:18:18.828
- [ Roaring ]
- Open the door!


01:18:18.899 --> 01:18:20.457
- Open the door!
- Open the door!


01:18:20.534 --> 01:18:24.231
- It's right behind you! Dad!
- [ All Screaming, Shouting ]


01:18:24.305 --> 01:18:26.068
[ Groaning ]


01:18:26.140 --> 01:18:28.836
- Dad!
- [ Roaring Continues ]


01:18:28.909 --> 01:18:30.638
Where did he go?


01:18:31.712 --> 01:18:33.680
- [ Screams ]
- Dad!


01:18:33.748 --> 01:18:35.909
Tom!


01:18:36.984 --> 01:18:39.976
- Where is he?
- [ David ] Dad!


01:18:40.054 --> 01:18:43.251
Tom! Where is he?


01:18:44.725 --> 01:18:47.023
- [ Roaring Continues ]
- [ Screams ]


01:18:47.094 --> 01:18:49.995
- Tom, are you down there?
- Yeah! I'm under the car!


01:18:50.064 --> 01:18:52.726
- Are you hurt?
- I'm fine!


01:18:54.135 --> 01:18:56.228
We need to do something.


01:18:56.303 --> 01:18:59.238
Yeah. Yeah. Okay.


01:18:59.306 --> 01:19:01.638
Where's that tool kit?


01:19:05.279 --> 01:19:08.077
Which side is the gas tank on?


01:19:08.149 --> 01:19:10.208
It's over here.


01:19:10.284 --> 01:19:12.878
I need you to put the seats back
the way they were.


01:19:12.953 --> 01:19:16.684
David, get me that lighter.


01:19:16.757 --> 01:19:19.282
[ Grunting ]


01:19:19.360 --> 01:19:22.295
Amy, what are you doing? Amy!


01:19:24.265 --> 01:19:26.893
[ Grunting, Screaming ]


01:19:38.279 --> 01:19:41.715
- What are you doing? That's gasoline!
- I know!


01:19:41.782 --> 01:19:44.808
[ Roaring Continues ]


01:19:51.292 --> 01:19:53.487
- You guys trust me?
- What?


01:19:53.561 --> 01:19:55.756
Do you trust me?


01:19:55.830 --> 01:19:58.355
- Yeah!
- Yes.


01:19:58.432 --> 01:20:00.400
You see that big tree out there?


01:20:00.468 --> 01:20:03.767
When I say so, I want you
to go out that front door...


01:20:03.838 --> 01:20:06.773
run to that tree and climb up it.


01:20:06.841 --> 01:20:09.332
But only when I say so. Okay?


01:20:09.410 --> 01:20:12.106
- Okay.
- Okay.


01:20:12.179 --> 01:20:14.238
- Tom!
- Yeah?


01:20:14.315 --> 01:20:19.014
When I say so, I want you to get
from underneath this car and run.


01:20:19.086 --> 01:20:23.113
The kids are going out the front door.
I want you to go with them.


01:20:23.190 --> 01:20:25.750
Let's do this. Okay?


01:20:27.528 --> 01:20:29.962
[ Roaring Continues ]


01:20:30.030 --> 01:20:32.521
Hey! Over here!


01:20:32.600 --> 01:20:36.661
Come on!
Come and get me! Come on!


01:20:36.737 --> 01:20:38.967
Now!


01:20:44.612 --> 01:20:46.512
David, come on!


01:20:47.681 --> 01:20:49.774
[ Roaring Continues ]


01:20:53.721 --> 01:20:56.952
Go up the tree.
Get all the way up the tree!


01:20:57.024 --> 01:20:59.254
[ Whimpering ]


01:21:00.027 --> 01:21:02.359
Amy! Get out of the car!


01:21:10.538 --> 01:21:12.802
- Dad! No!
- Amy!


01:21:17.378 --> 01:21:19.869
[ Roaring ]


01:23:33.814 --> 01:23:35.975
Let's go home.

